   "building_id": "B60_balance",
   "sector_id": "S03_market",
   "alt": "The great weighing hall of the market, painted in ink and gouache: an open arched gateway on the left leads back to the market square; six colored doors stand side by side in the back wall: red, yellow and green arched doors, then blue, purple and teal doors. A boy cuts a pie into equal portions, a line of small children carry slices of cake, a baker holds a heavy mass of dough beside a brass balance, a hundred balloons float up, a little boy heaves a whole cheese with a teacup on top, a girl checks her spirit level on her knee, a dog sleeps on the leftover bread, a thermometer climbs in gray steam, a boy cheers at a jar of marbles, a little girl hugs one piece of cheese, a tall golden sheaf of wheat wears a tag with the digit 7 and a girl cuts an apple in half.",
   "nameplate": [
    57,
    10
   ]
