   "building_id": "B60_balance",
   "sector_id": "S03_market",
   "alt": "The room of scales: through a wide cream-stone arch under the green-iron glass roof, everyone crowds round a giant brass beam balance. A baker pours more and more flour so the dial pointer springs off the end, a heap of chocolate bends the other pan down, a tabby cat pushes her old bowl away, a pigeon bows over a heap of seeds, twin girls each hold a red balloon, a waiter carries a very tall cupcake tower, a stuffed green troll's belt bursts open, a little astronaut points at a model Pluto, a cook squeezes a garlic press and a tiny toy train puffs once. At the front sits the vegetable crate with its paper scroll. A red door leads back to the hall; steps lead up to the yellow door of the weighing room.",
