   "building_id": "B60_balance",
   "sector_id": "S03_market",
   "alt": "The weighing yard: a cream-stone courtyard with red tile roofs under a glass dome on green iron arches, busy with weighing. A gray elephant makes the floor weighbridge tremble, a nervous goat shakes on a platform scale, a boy heaves an anvil over his head and another presses down with all his might on a kitchen scale. A man sits so heavily that his chair snaps, a cozy man finishes his jigsaw, a fluffy cat on a cushion is almost asleep, two cats weigh themselves one sitting and one sprawled, a dormouse sleeps deep in walnuts, a cake stand holds only crumbs beside a guilty dog, a full mouse lies on his back in an empty pan, lemonade fizzes over, a sad man sits under two bare trees, a tall uncle stands beside a tiny girl and a tool rack holds one lonely spanner. A yellow door leads back to the hall and a green door up to the loft.",
